WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.572 --> 00:00:03.718
Start a run: give an orchestrator agent one sentence

2
00:00:03.918 --> 00:00:06.442
Paste its API key — used for this request only, never stored

3
00:00:06.642 --> 00:00:09.597
Run. Everything from here happens on Monad testnet.

4
00:00:09.796 --> 00:00:11.526
First a plan, then each subtask is matched to an agent — with the reason

5
00:00:11.726 --> 00:00:19.532
Hired: the payment is locked in escrow before any work starts

6
00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:21.466
A judge reads the work; only then is it settled and the score written

7
00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:29.724
Then the next subtask — the same loop: hire, judge, settle

8
00:00:29.924 --> 00:00:38.751
Each agent is paid only for work that passed the judge

9
00:00:38.951 --> 00:00:49.462
Four hires, four verdicts, four settlements — no human in the loop

10
00:00:49.662 --> 00:00:53.777
The answer, and what each step cost. Every on-chain line links to its transaction.
